//@version=6
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// H Ticks B — TAP + TRIGGER : a 15m / 1H / 4H gap is TAPPED in the bias direction -> a later 1m or 2m FVG inverts in that
//                              direction -> entry at the close of the candle that processes it -> stop beyond the inversion
//                              candle -> target exactly 1R.     (Indicator B. Indicator A is the 30s chain, a separate script.)
// REQUIRES A STANDARD 30-SECOND CHART. Anything else shows "Switch to a standard 30-second chart" and generates nothing.
//   1. BIAS: the chosen Bias source (15m structure / 4H structure / VWAP / EMAs), or OFF with the Relaxed tickbox.
//   2. TAP (arms): a tracked 15m/1H/4H gap, pointing the SAME way as the bias, is first touched by price inside an enabled
//      entry window. One tap is armed at a time. The arm ends at the window end, at a bias flip, or at an entry.
//   3. TRIGGER: a 1m or 2m source FVG inverts (confirmed close through its far boundary, at least the minimum gap size) in the
//      armed direction; its source candle must OPEN at/after the tap candle closed, inside the same window instance.
//   4. CONFLUENCE (optional): VWAP side, EMA 9/21 trend, or both (see settings). A failed trigger leaves the arm in place.
//   5. STOP = beyond the extreme of the inverting 1m/2m candle +/- max(1 tick, 0.10 x previous 30s ATR); ENTRY = close of the
//      30s candle that processes the trigger; TARGET = same tick distance (1R). Trades with risk above the max-risk setting are skipped.
//   6. CLEAR PATH (optional, default ON): no opposing 15m/1H/4H gap on [entry, target] and the target ends >= 1 tick before the
//      nearest unconsumed 3m swing level. Missing coverage is UNKNOWN, never clear.
//   Gates: same window instance, < 3 entries per instance, one unresolved setup at a time.
// Verification: code review + text checks only. NOT compiled in TradingView, NOT Bar-Replay tested. No win-rate claim.
// ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// INDICATOR (not a strategy). Outcomes: OPEN / TARGET_HIT / STOP_HIT / AMBIGUOUS on 30s candles strictly AFTER the entry
// candle (opening price first, then the range). No slippage, costs or time exit; an estimate, not broker results.
indicator("H Ticks B — Tap + Trigger", shorttitle = "H Ticks B", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_bars_back = 500)

const string GRP_CTX = "Context timeframe"
const string GRP_WIN = "Entry windows (Asia 09:00 Tokyo -> 08:00 London, NY 09:45-11:30, NY 14:30-15:30; DST-aware; Mon-Fri)"
const string GRP_Q   = "Setup quality"
const string GRP_BIAS = "Directional bias"
const string GRP_APP = "Chart appearance"
const string GRP_ST  = "Statistics"
const string GRP_DBG = "Debug"
const string GRP_AL  = "Alerts"
string inCtxSel = input.string("Auto (1m, 2m)", "Trigger timeframe", options = ["Auto (1m, 2m)", "1m only", "2m only"], group = GRP_CTX, tooltip = "Which source timeframes may supply the trigger inversion. Auto: either a 1m or a 2m inversion (whichever comes first).")
bool   inRelaxWin = input.bool(false, "Relaxed: allow ALL hours (ignore the windows above)", group = GRP_WIN, tooltip = "OFF = original windows. ON = contexts and entries are accepted at any time Mon-Fri; the whole New York trading day (18:00 to 18:00) is ONE window instance with the usual entry limit, so a context can live until 18:00 NY. Stats then count every bar under the 'outside any window' row.")
bool   inWinAsia = input.bool(true, "Window A: Asia open -> London open", group = GRP_WIN)
bool   inWinAm = input.bool(true, "Window B: New York morning 09:45-11:30", group = GRP_WIN, tooltip = "Start inclusive, end exclusive. BOTH the context inversion and the entry must belong to the same window instance (max 3 entries per instance, one unresolved setup at a time).")
bool   inWinPm = input.bool(true, "Window C: New York afternoon 14:30-15:30", group = GRP_WIN)
int    inMinTick = input.int(1, "Minimum gap size (ticks, all gap sources)", minval = 1, group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "Gaps at least this wide are detected and may form contexts, triggers and obstacles.")
bool   inNoBias = input.bool(false, "Relaxed: turn the directional bias OFF", group = GRP_BIAS, tooltip = "OFF = original behaviour. ON = contexts of either direction are accepted, a bias flip never cancels a context and the entry does not check the bias. The bias source below is then ignored and the stats show the bias as OFF.")
string inBiasSrc = input.string("15m structure", "Bias source", options = ["15m structure", "4H structure", "VWAP", "EMAs"], group = GRP_BIAS, tooltip = "Which direction filter a context must agree with. 15m structure = the original swing-break bias (default). 4H structure = the same engine on 4H candles (slow; needs many days of loaded history). VWAP = daily-session VWAP: bullish above, bearish below. EMAs = on 5m: bullish when price > fast EMA > slow EMA, bearish when price < fast < slow, otherwise no bias. If the bias flips against a pending context, that context is cancelled.")
int    inEmaF = input.int(21, "EMA fast length (5m, used by EMAs)", minval = 1, group = GRP_BIAS)
int    inEmaS = input.int(50, "EMA slow length (5m, used by EMAs)", minval = 2, group = GRP_BIAS)
int    inMaxRisk = input.int(80, "Maximum risk (ticks); wider setups are skipped", minval = 4, group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "Risk = entry to stop. NQ: 4 ticks = 1 point. 80 ticks = 20 points.")
string inConf = input.string("None", "Confluence at the trigger", options = ["None", "VWAP side", "EMA 9/21 trend", "VWAP + EMA stack"], group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "None = off. VWAP side: close above (long) / below (short) the NY-09:30-anchored VWAP. EMA 9/21 trend: 1m EMA9 above/below EMA21. VWAP + EMA stack: VWAP side AND close beyond both EMAs with EMA9 beyond EMA21. Evaluated at the trigger, not at the tap.")
bool   inClear = input.bool(true, "Require a clear path to 1R (HTF gaps + 3m swing)", group = GRP_Q, tooltip = "ON = skip the setup if an opposing 15m/1H/4H gap or an unconsumed 3m swing level sits between entry and the 1R target (unknown coverage also skips). OFF = no path check.")
bool   inShowPair = input.bool(true, "Show the context gap + 30s trigger gap of every setup", group = GRP_APP)
bool   inShowHtf = input.bool(false, "Show nearby HTF gap boxes (clutter; OFF by default)", group = GRP_APP, tooltip = "Display only. Obstacle checks ALWAYS use all tracked 15m/1H/4H gaps, shown or hidden.")
bool   inShowMarkers = input.bool(false, "Show detail markers (retest, stop anchor, inversion candles)", group = GRP_APP, tooltip = "Small labels that explain how a setup formed. The same facts are always in the label tooltips.")
bool   inShowRR = input.bool(true, "Show risk/reward shading", group = GRP_APP)
string inTheme = input.string("Light", "Theme (labels and tables)", options = ["Light", "Dark"], group = GRP_APP, tooltip = "Light: black entry line. Dark: white entry line (black would be invisible). Tables always use opaque backgrounds.")
bool   inStats = input.bool(true, "Show the small stats box (top-right)", group = GRP_ST)
bool   inDaily = input.bool(false, "Optional: daily breakdown under the stats box", group = GRP_ST)
int    inRepDays = input.int(20, "Days reported (stats box and debug counts)", minval = 1, maxval = 20, group = GRP_ST, tooltip = "How many of the latest Mon-Fri New York dates the stats box and the debug counts cover. If the chart has fewer dates loaded, everything available is used and Coverage reads Partial. TradingView limits how many 30s bars are loaded; the script cannot add more.")
bool   inDebug = input.bool(false, "Debug panel: per-date / per-session funnel, first failed gate, lock intervals, source readiness, rejection records", group = GRP_DBG, tooltip = "Counts cover the reported NY dates (setting: Days reported). Every rejected candidate is counted once at its FIRST failed gate and written to Pine Logs with timestamps, source timeframe and measured value vs threshold.")
bool   alEntry = input.bool(true, "Alert on each new entry", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alTarget = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its target", group = GRP_AL)
bool   alStop = input.bool(true, "Alert when a setup hits its stop", group = GRP_AL)

